<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean firms seek 102,500 tonnes of corn - traders.</title>
<headline>S.Korean firms seek 102,500 tonnes of corn - traders.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group of South Korean feed mill companies invited tenders on Tuesday to buy a total of 102,500 tonnes of corn, traders said.</p>
<p>They said the group included Cheiljedang Corp, Miwon Co Ltd, Woo Sung Feed Mill Co Ltd and Purina Korea, but declined to give more details.  </p>
<p>Traders said the companies were seeking the amount in two positions, with details as follows:</p>
<p> POSITION TONNE   SHIPMENT		   ETA/PORT</p>
<p>   One    52,500  Apr 6-25 (Argentine)   May 30/Inchon or Ulsan</p>
<p>			Apr 26-May 15 (PNW)	     &quot;</p>
<p>			Apr 10-30 (Gulf)		  &quot;</p>
<p>   Two    50,000  Apr 27-May 16 (Argen)  June 20/Inchon</p>
<p>			May 17-Jun 5  (PNW)	     &quot;</p>
<p>			May 2-21 (Gulf)		   &quot;</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
